+    post-conv inputs (the wide scratch's saves, free while no step runs) and they scatter to buffer rows h..h+R at
+    the device h; when the window would overflow (h + R > L) the committed rows flush into the other parity's
+    checkpoint with a fixed L-row replay -- rows h..L-1 are neutral (``_replay_neutral``), so its bits are the serial
+    steps over rows 0..h-1 exactly -- then out_only reads the round's outputs from the checkpoint + buffer with no
+    state write (h from the device mirror, so a captured graph serves any h) and the wide path's out_kernel norms
+    the read-out. A rejected draft's commit is a buffer-pointer move (``commit``)."""
+
+    c = w.cfg
+    k = layer.kda
+    L = kda_mod.REPLAY_LEN
+    s = st.scratch[li]
+    flush = st.rb_h + R > L
